---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/site";
import { cliSession, toHtml } from "../lib/cli-demo";
import tuiShot from "../../../docs/screenshots/tui-list-dark.png";
import appDark from "../assets/ui/app-graph-dark.png";
import appLight from "../assets/ui/app-graph-light.png";

const tabs = [
  { key: "cli", label: "CLI", icon: "Terminal" },
  { key: "tui", label: "TUI", icon: "SquareTerminal" },
  { key: "desktop", label: "Desktop", icon: "Monitor" },
  { key: "mcp", label: "MCP", icon: "Bot" },
];
const mcpJson = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "portwise": { "command": "portwise", "args": ["mcp"] }
  }
}`;
const sizes = "(max-width: 900px) calc(100vw - 40px), 640px";
---
<section id="interfaces" class="section" aria-labelledby="if-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Interfaces</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="if-title">One core. <span class="soft">Four ways in.</span></h2>
      <p class="lede">The same Rust core decides who owns a port and whether it's safe to touch. Each interface only renders and confirms what it says.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Interfaces" data-tabs>
      {tabs.map((t, i) => (
        <button type="button" role="tab" id={`if-tab-${t.key}`} aria-controls={`if-${t.key}`} aria-selected={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"} tabindex={i === 0 ? 0 : -1} data-key={t.key}>
          <Icon name={t.icon} size={16} /> {t.label}
        </button>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="if-cli" aria-labelledby="if-tab-cli">
      <div class="text">
        <h3>A scriptable CLI</h3>
        <p>Look, act, wait and free ports from any shell or script — and see which agents and tools started them. Plain-English answers for people, <code>--json</code> for tools, and exit codes that mean something.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><code>portwise agents</code> maps agents, tools and apps to their footprint</li>
          <li><code>portwise agents claude --stop-ports</code> stops only what that agent started</li>
          <li><code>portwise explain 3000</code> says who holds it and what to do</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="link-arrow" href={url("docs/cli/")}>CLI reference <Icon name="ArrowRight" size={16} /></a>
      </div>
      <figure class="visual term-window">
        <div class="window-bar"><span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="window-title">~/code/shop-web</span></div>
        <pre class="term cli-term" aria-label="portwise explain, wait and free-port in a terminal"><code set:html={cliSession.map(toHtml).join("\n")} /></pre>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="if-tui" aria-labelledby="if-tab-tui" hidden>
      <div class="text">
        <h3>A TUI that stays out of the way</h3>
        <p>Run <code>portwise</code> with no arguments. Arrow through ports, filter as you type, browse the Agents tab, and stop with a confirm — all from the keyboard.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Same details as the desktop app: tree, memory, connections</li>
          <li>Tab cycles Ports → Graph → Agents; <kbd>x</kbd> stops an agent’s ports</li>
          <li>Works over SSH sessions and in tmux</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="visual window tui"><Picture src={tuiShot} formats={["avif"]} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[640, 1374]} sizes={sizes} alt="The portwise TUI: a port table with the details pane for the selected port" loading="lazy" /></figure>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="if-desktop" aria-labelledby="if-tab-desktop" hidden>
      <div class="text">
        <h3>A desktop and tray app</h3>
        <p>The port list, details, the service graph, the agents map, pins, history with one-click restart and remote hosts over SSH. <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>⌥</kbd><kbd>P</kbd> brings it up from any app.</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>Agents map on <kbd>⇧</kbd><kbd>A</kbd>: mem, CPU, folders, access, stop what they started</li>
          <li>Command palette on <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>K</kbd> / <kbd>Ctrl</kbd><kbd>K</kbd></li>
          <li>Reveal a folder, open it in your editor, or stop that agent’s ports</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="link-arrow" href={url("#demo")}>Try it live <Icon name="ArrowRight" size={16} /></a>
      </div>
      <figure class="visual window">
        <Picture src={appDark} formats={["avif"]} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[640, 1280, 1920]} sizes={sizes} alt="The desktop app's service graph: a Compose cluster with shop-web, shop-api, db and redis" loading="lazy" pictureAttributes={{ class: "only-dark" }} />
        <Picture src={appLight} formats={["avif"]} fallbackFormat="webp" widths={[640, 1280, 1920]} sizes={sizes} alt="The desktop app's service graph: a Compose cluster with shop-web, shop-api, db and redis" loading="lazy" pictureAttributes={{ class: "only-light" }} />
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="if-mcp" aria-labelledby="if-tab-mcp" hidden>
      <div class="text">
        <h3>An MCP server for AI agents</h3>
        <p><code>portwise mcp</code> gives coding assistants nine tools: list, explain, find a free port, wait, read the graph, see which agents and tools run where, stop the ports an agent started, plan a cluster stop (dry run only) and stop their own dev servers. Protected processes are always refused.</p>
        <div class="code term-window">
          <div class="code-bar"><span>~/.cursor/mcp.json</span><button type="button" class="copy" data-copy={mcpJson} aria-label="Copy the MCP configuration"><Icon name="Copy" size={14} class="i-copy" /><Icon name="Check" size={14} class="i-done" /></button></div>
          <pre><code>{mcpJson}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <a class="link-arrow" href={url("docs/mcp/")}>Set up Claude, Cursor or VS Code <Icon name="ArrowRight" size={16} /></a>
      </div>
      <figure class="visual chat" aria-label="An AI agent using portwise tools">
        <div class="msg user">Which agent started the server on 3001?</div>
        <div class="tool"><Icon name="Wrench" size={14} /> list_agents <span>{"{}"}</span></div>
        <div class="msg agent"><b>Claude Code</b> holds <code>:3001</code> (Vite · shop-api), 214&nbsp;MB, 1 stoppable port. Access: sandbox unknown.</div>
        <div class="tool"><Icon name="Wrench" size={14} /> stop_agent_ports <span>{"{ agent: \"claude\", dry_run: true }"}</span></div>
        <div class="msg agent"><span class="ok">✔</span> Plan: stop the Vite tree on :3001. Nothing changed (dry run).</div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .tabs { display: flex; gap: 24px; margin: 0 0 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); overflow-x: auto; scrollbar-width: none; }
  .tabs button {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; height: 44px; padding: 0; margin-bottom: -1px; border: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    background: transparent; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--fs-md); font-weight: 500; cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
    transition: color 140ms, border-color 140ms;
  }
  .tabs button :global(svg) { flex: none; }
  .tabs button:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .tabs button[aria-selected="true"] { color: var(--text); border-bottom-color: var(--text); }
  .panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: 64px; align-items: center; }
  .panel[hidden] { display: none; }
  h3 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: var(--fs-xl); line-height: 28px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
  .text > p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--fs-md); line-height: 24px; }
  .ticks { list-style: none; margin: 24px 0 0; padding: 24px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); display: grid; gap: 12px; color: var(--text-2); font-size: var(--fs-md); line-height: 24px; }
  .ticks li { position: relative; padding-left: 20px; }
  .ticks li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 2px; top: 10px; width: 4px; height: 4px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--muted); }
  .text .link-arrow { margin-top: 24px; }
  .visual { margin: 0; }
  .visual :global(img) { width: 100%; }
  kbd { margin: 0 1px; }
  .code { margin-top: 24px; }
  .code-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; height: 40px; padding: 0 4px 0 16px; font: 12px var(--mono); color: var(--term-dim); background: var(--term-bar); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--term-line); }
  .code pre { margin: 0; padding: 16px; font-size: var(--fs-sm); line-height: var(--lh-code); color: var(--term-text); overflow-x: auto; font-variant-ligatures: none; }
  .code pre code { background: none; padding: 0; color: inherit; font-size: inherit; }
  .copy { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: var(--r-xs); border: 0; background: transparent; color: var(--term-dim); cursor: pointer; }
  .copy:hover { color: var(--term-text); }
  .copy :global(.i-done) { display: none; color: var(--green); }
  .copy[data-copied] :global(.i-done) { display: block; }
  .copy[data-copied] :global(.i-copy) { display: none; }
  .chat { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; padding: 32px; border-radius: var(--r-md); background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: var(--fs-md); line-height: 24px; }
  .msg { max-width: 88%; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: var(--r-md); }
  .user { align-self: flex-end; background: var(--surface-3); color: var(--text); }
  .agent { color: var(--text-2); padding-left: 0; }
  .agent code { font-size: 0.875em; }
  .ok { color: var(--green); }
  .tool { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; width: fit-content; height: 28px; padding: 0 12px; border-radius: var(--r-xs); font: 500 var(--fs-xs) var(--mono); color: var(--muted); background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .tool span { color: var(--text-2); }
  .cli-term { margin: 0; padding: 16px 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .panel { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 40px; } }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .tabs { gap: 20px; } }
</style>
